{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And repays His enemies, etc.</b> It is difficult: why did He say <b>His enemies</b> in the plural and conclude by saying <b>to His face, to destroy him</b> in the singular? And perhaps the reason He said it in the plural is that He does not repay the wicked to his face except when He sees that it is not he alone who hates, but also those who come from him are like him — for in this case he has no hope, and that is what is meant by <b>and repays His enemies</b> in the plural. But if he alone is the enemy, and his offspring that comes from him will not be an enemy — a righteous son can merit the father — and He will not repay him to destroy him." "<b>And it concludes</b> by speaking in the singular, for Scripture is speaking of an individual, only it alerted you through what was said in that He said <b>His enemies</b> in the plural, and then returned to say <b>He will not delay</b>, etc. — meaning: and if the wicked does not come as a multitude but is alone an enemy, and those who come after him are not, HaShem will deal wisely with him in another manner and will not delay his punishment in this world, so that he does not sin further and his hope be lost; rather, He will hasten to pay him the death he is liable for, or suffering, since there is hope that he may be merited through the merit of his son." "And His saying <b>to His face</b> — this is along the lines of what they said, of blessed memory (Yerushalmi Avodah Zarah 3:1[5]), that the righteous, near their death, HaShem gives them a taste of their world to come, and their soul is sated and they sleep out of joy, whereas the wicked are shown the evil awaiting them before they depart from the world (Esther Rabbah, parashat VaTikhal HaMalka, 2), and that is what is meant by <b>He will not delay to repay His enemy to His face</b> — meaning, in this world, before his face is buried in the dust, He will show him his recompense and will not delay until he arrives there." "<b>Thus concludes the parashah of Va'etchanan.</b>"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:15:47.334923126Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}